# Profile: train_off -- the CROSS arm alone, with the distance trigger disabled.
#
# WHY (measured, 2026-09-16). The TRAIN arm is a high-WIN-RATE arm and that is
# exactly why it loses money. It buys deep in-the-money favourites, so it wins
# often and the win rate looks good in isolation -- but you pay for that win
# rate in the price, and the price is where the money goes:
#
#     breakeven win rate  =  price + fee
#
#     0.82 -> need 83.0%     0.85 -> need 86.0%
#
# Live record, 40 fires: it PAID 0.8361 and won 72.0%. Required: 84.6%.
# EV -0.1182/share resting, -0.0263/share even taking at the fire instant.
# The bands are non-monotone (0.84-0.86 +0.0519 next to 0.80-0.84 -0.2346) and
# the losers cluster by TIME, not price, which is the signature of a level
# condition firing into a drift rather than an edge.
#
# So "disable it because its PnL is low" is the right call, and the reason is
# sharper than low PnL: at the prices it pays, a 72% win rate is a LOSING bet.
#
# WHAT IS LEFT after this profile: the CROSS arm (cross_enabled=true), which
# fires on a spot crossing the strike inside the 5-60s tau window. The MAIN
# model arm is switched separately (see model_mode) and is NOT touched here.
#
# Revert with:  make config PROFILE=... (the switch backs .env up first)
cross_train_enabled=false
